<div id="p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="p2.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_center"><span id="p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Appendices of “Toward a Unified Framework for Data-
Efficient Evaluation of Large Language Models”</span></p>
</div>
<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_font_bold ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix"><span id="A1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">Appendix A</span> </span>Disclosure: Use of LLMs</h2>

<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">LLMs are used as an assistant in this project. Specifically, LLMs are used for</span></p>
<ul id="A1.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A1.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Polish writing: Refine statements, improve fluency.</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Coding assistance: Help draft prototype codes and alleviate engineering efforts.</span></p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_font_bold ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix"><span id="A2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">Appendix B</span> </span>Experimental details</h2>

<section id="A2.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_font_bold ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection"><span id="A2.SS1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">B.1</span> </span>Benchmarks and models</h3>

<div id="A2.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">A summary for all five datasets we used is reported in table </span><a href="#A2.T4" title="Table 4 ‣ B.1 Benchmarks and models ‣ Appendix B Experimental details ‣ Toward a unified framework fordata-efficient evaluation oflarge language models" class="ltx_ref ltx_font_bold"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a></p>
</div>
<figure id="A2.T4" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering ltx_font_bold"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="A2.T4.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">Table 4</span>: </span>Summary statistics for the evaluation benchmarks. MCQ denotes <em id="A2.T4.8" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic"><span id="A2.T4.8.1" class="ltx_text ltx_underline ltx_font_upright">M</span><span id="A2.T4.8.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_upright">ultiple <span id="A2.T4.8.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_underline">C</span>hoice <span id="A2.T4.8.2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_underline">Q</span>uestion</span></em>, NLG denotes <em id="A2.T4.9" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic"><span id="A2.T4.9.1" class="ltx_text ltx_underline ltx_font_upright">N</span><span id="A2.T4.9.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_upright">atural <span id="A2.T4.9.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_underline">L</span>anguage <span id="A2.T4.9.2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_underline">G</span>eneration</span></em></figcaption>
<table id="A2.T4.10" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
